# CLAUDE.md — TEMPLATE FOR YOU TO AUTHOR

Author this file in M2.S3. Rename to `CLAUDE.md` when done. Six required sections:

## Stack
<!-- Python 3.11+, FastAPI 0.115, SQLAlchemy 2.0 (select() — never query()), aiosqlite, pytest 8 + pytest-asyncio (asyncio_mode=auto), pydantic 2 — Pydantic v2 syntax (model_validate, not .from_orm). -->

## Conventions
<!-- snake_case modules + functions, PascalCase classes, mandatory `from __future__ import annotations`, type hints required, async-first, constructor injection (no global state), httpx.AsyncClient for HTTP. -->

## Testing
<!-- pytest 8 + pytest-asyncio. NEVER unittest.TestCase. Mocks: pytest-mock + AsyncMock for async paths. Fixtures in conftest.py. Coverage target ≥85%. -->

## Don't-Touch
<!-- - .env / application-prod.* config
     - alembic/versions/*.py — never modify in place; ADD a new revision
     - app/db.py engine / session config without explicit approval
     - tests/conftest.py fixture order (it's a smell of test pollution) -->

## Commands
<!-- Run tests:    pytest -v
     Lint:         ruff check app/
     Type-check:   mypy app/
     Run local:    uvicorn app.main:app --reload -->

## Escalation
<!-- When should Claude STOP and ask a human?
     - Schema changes (new alembic revision, altered column type)
     - Any change to authentication / authorization
     - New dependency in requirements.txt
     - Removing a test without replacing it -->
